Description: Fix crash with gradient background-image in the GTK theme
 panel_background_prepare() passes an uninitialized pointer to
 cairo_pattern_get_surface() and ignores its return value. For a pattern
 that is not a surface pattern, such as the one GTK returns for
 background-image: -gtk-gradient(...), cairo_pattern_get_surface() fails
 with CAIRO_STATUS_PATTERN_TYPE_MISMATCH and does not set the pointer. The
 check "surface != NULL", meant to catch exactly this case, then tests
 uninitialized stack memory, and mate-panel crashes in
 cairo_surface_reference() (SIGSEGV or a cairo assertion) or later in
 gdk_window_set_background_pattern(), depending on the stack contents.
 .
 Initialize the pointer and check the return value, so such a theme falls
 back to the background color with the existing warning, as intended.
 .
 Reproducer: GTK theme Blackbird (package blackbird-gtk-theme), which sets
 background-image: -gtk-gradient(...) for PanelToplevel.
Author: Armin Fuerst <armin@fuerst.priv.at>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-10-10
---
--- a/mate-panel/panel-background.c	2026-10-10 18:17:20.979260128 +0000
+++ b/mate-panel/panel-background.c	2026-10-10 18:17:21.045607285 +0000
@@ -101,10 +101,13 @@
 			* backing region is cleared
 			* (gdk_window_clear_backing_region), the correctly
 			* scaled pattern is used */
-			cairo_surface_t *surface;
+			cairo_surface_t *surface = NULL;
 
-			cairo_pattern_get_surface(background->default_pattern, &surface);
-			/* catch invalid images (e.g. -gtk-gradient) before scaling and rendering */
+			/* catch invalid images (e.g. -gtk-gradient) before scaling and rendering:
+			 * for a pattern that is not a surface pattern, such as a gradient,
+			 * cairo_pattern_get_surface() fails and leaves surface unset */
+			if (cairo_pattern_get_surface (background->default_pattern, &surface) != CAIRO_STATUS_SUCCESS)
+				surface = NULL;
 			if (surface != NULL ){
 				double width, height;
 				cairo_matrix_t m;
